  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<math> <mrow> <msup> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">EDTA</mtext> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> <mo>-</mo> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;is ethylenediaminetetraacetate ion. The total number of N - Co - O bond angles in <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">Co</mtext> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">EDTA</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mo>-</mo> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;complex ion is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>EDTA</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>  is a hexadentate ligand containing four negative charges on its corner oxygen atoms as follows :</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/Untitledhexad.png\"/></p><p> </p><p>Being a hexadentate ligand, it forms a ring like structure through chelation.</p><p> </p><p> </p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/EM00012588_AnsExp1_2.jpg\"/></p><p> </p><p>The central metal ion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Co</mi></math> is in the centre, coordinated to the two <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> atoms and the four <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math> ions through chelation. Now, if we observe, we see that each <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> atom forms four <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo> </mo><mo>-</mo><mo> </mo><mi>Co</mi><mo> </mo><mo>-</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> bonds with the four <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math> ions. Therefore, two <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> atoms will form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mo>×</mo><mo> </mo><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mn>8</mn></math>  <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo> </mo><mo>-</mo><mo> </mo><mi>Co</mi><mo> </mo><mo>-</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> bonds in the complex structure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>EDTA</mi><mo>)</mo><msup><mo>]</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>. Each bond will have a certain bond angle. Hence, it can be concluded that the total number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo> </mo><mo>-</mo><mo> </mo><mi>Co</mi><mo> </mo><mo>-</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> bond angles in the complex ion is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math>.</p><p> </p>",
    "image": null
  },
